<.timeline_entry
  logo="/images/derivco.png"
  logo_alt="Derivco logo"
  title="Derivco"
  role="Software Developer"
  start_date={~D[2019-05-01]}
  end_date={~D[2020-02-01]}
  highlights={[
    "Migrated a microservice from Ruby to Elixir, forwarding core database changes through RabbitMQ",
    "Part of the Core team, maintaining services in Ruby, Elixir and Go"
  ]}
  details_id="more-information-derivco"
  details={[
    "After working for a tiny startup for almost three years, I wanted to try a bigger company while continuing to work with Elixir. That's why I decided to join Derivco, a company with more than 4,000 employees worldwide and the software provider for Betway, one of the biggest sportsbooks in the world.",
    "<strong>At Derivco, I was part of the Core team, in charge of developing and maintaining several services in Ruby, Elixir and Go.</strong>",
    "One of the main projects I worked on was the migration of a microservice from Ruby to Elixir. This service forwarded changes from the core database, using triggers to listen for changes and RabbitMQ as the message broker."
  ]}
>
